# Primary literature and actual scope

Burgarth, Bose, Bruder and Giovannetti, *Local controllability of quantum networks*, Physical Review A 79, 060305 (2009), DOI https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.79.060305; exact arXiv revision https://arxiv.org/abs/0805.3975v2, PDF https://arxiv.org/pdf/0805.3975v2.

The web-extracted complete four-page v2 text was read during initial route exploration. Its graph-infection and algebraic-propagation theorem, and Heisenberg-chain endpoint example, were inspected. The paper assumes an externally controllable local set; it does not supply the finite prepared autonomous controller required here. Its pure-chain criterion is not applied directly to arbitrary H plus extra edges. The new derivation gives the Pauli induction and separate polynomial argument explicitly. References cited by that paper were not read or imported. No full-figure or experimental audit is claimed.

